`ObjectForm` component remained in loading state indefinitely when `mode='create'`, preventing form fields from rendering. Test `ObjectForm.msw.test.tsx` failed waiting for form fields to appear.

## Changes

- **ObjectForm.tsx**: Added missing `setLoading(false)` in create mode early return path
  - `fetchInitialData` useEffect returned early for create mode without clearing loading state
  - Form remained stuck showing "Loading form..." spinner

- **form.tsx**: Extracted schema props before spreading to DOM element
  - Prevented React warnings: `submitLabel`, `cancelLabel`, `showSubmit`, `showCancel`, `resetOnSubmit`, `defaultValues`, `inputType` were being spread to `<form>` DOM element
  - Props now destructured and ignored, only valid DOM props spread via `{...formProps}`

```tsx
// Before: loading state never cleared in create mode
if (!schema.recordId || schema.mode === 'create') {
  setInitialData(schema.initialData || schema.initialValues || {});
  return; // ❌ exits without setLoading(false)
}

// After: loading state properly cleared
if (!schema.recordId || schema.mode === 'create') {
  setInitialData(schema.initialData || schema.initialValues || {});
  setLoading(false); // ✅ form renders
  return;
}
```

